# sdrpp-git is deliberately excluded — currently broken. Its makedepends
# unconditionally builds every optional SDR backend (_plugindeps), one of
# which is libsdrplay, whose PKGBUILD downloads a vendor .run installer
# from sdrplay.com that now 404s. Blocks the whole AUR batch if left in;
# see notes/pentest-tools.md "Gaps, currently broken" before re-adding.

# recon-ng and autopsy are deliberately excluded — both have currently-
# broken AUR PKGBUILDs (unresolvable deps: python-flasgger has no AUR
# package; java-openjfx=17 has aged out of the AUR). See
# notes/pentest-tools.md "Gaps, currently broken" before re-adding either.

# armitage-git, sliver, theharvester-git, powershell-empire-git, and
# wfuzz are NOT in this list even though they're part of the toolkit —
# all five need a build-scoped override (JDK 11, pinned Go toolchain, a
# pinned flit_core via PYTHONPATH, a mise-PATH-clean poetry build, a
# source patch for wfuzz's dropped pkg_resources import) that would be
# wrong to apply to the whole batch above. Installed by their own leaf
# scripts instead: see install/packages/aur-armitage.sh, aur-sliver.sh,
# aur-theharvester.sh, aur-powershell-empire.sh, aur-wfuzz.sh.

# beef in the list above is beef-xss (the real Browser Exploitation
# Framework) — a same-named-but-wrong AUR package called plain `beef` is
# a Brainfuck interpreter, not a security tool. beef-xss's PKGBUILD
# declares conflicts=('beef' 'beef-git'), so pacman/yay will prompt to
# remove the wrong package as part of this install if it's already on
# the system (confirmed via the real PKGBUILD, not guessed).

# AI Tools category has no package here yet — hexstrike-ai and garak are
# both git-clone/pip installs, not `omarchy pkg` targets. See
# notes/pentest-tools.md "AI Tools" section before adding a venv/pipx step.
